 is a war it's a very dynamic war  and of course in those areas where  russians have focused and concentrated  all of their firepower firing tens of  thousands of artillery shells a day of  course it is it makes sense for  ukrainian armed forces because we value  human life to retreat temporarily but in  other areas we are already  counter-attacking and providing we  receive more heavy weaponry soon we will  be able to do it even more efficiently  i think you bring us on to my next  question which was you talk about these  losses as being temporary how do you  reverse them  you reverse them by  receiving sufficient number of heavy  artillery  multi-launch rocket systems tanks  aircraft air defense systems anti-rocket  systems everything that our  international partners have committed to  provide us with and you do it militarily  so you you you you've been singing the  same song if i can put it that way for  for some months now that bring us uh uh  more uh heavy weaponry and this despite  promises from the likes of the united  states uh united kingdom  and germany to do just that  are they just not arriving quick enough  for you  some of the heavy weaponry that we have  been promised  by the united states  by germany by the uk has already arrived  in ukraine and is efficiently being used  on the front lines and we are very  grateful to our international partners  all of those who have gathered at  ramstein at nato summit recently and  they have committed themselves  wholeheartedly to support ukraine  militarily for as long as it takes but  of course  you know us and  on the battlefield we need we understand  that we need more heavy weaponry and we  need it faster and we hope that our  partners will find ways to deliver us  this  vital military assistance sooner rather  than later  and so now as russia  secures uh its hold on the the east of  ukraine where do you expect it to turn  its uh its firepower next what do you  expect it's its next target to be  well first of all russia has not yet  established its hold on the east of  ukraine because there's still donetsk  region and there are cities such as  slavyansk they've been mentioned in your  report earlier there is a city of  kramatorsk and there are very capable  highly motivated and professional  ukrainian armed forces which are located  there and they will continue resistance  and actually these cities the slovakian  cremators are most likely to be the next  major  the next major objective military  objective of the russian aggressor but  the major the key overarching military  objective of the aggressor has always  been to encircle ukrainian armed forces  in the east of ukraine and destroy them  and this has not happened this has not  happened because even from listed chance  ukrainian armed forces have been able to  retreat without losses so from that  perspective we understand where the next  target will be but we also understand  that we are doing everything we can in  terms of tactics and maneuvers to ensure  that we incur as much losses on our  enemy as possible and at the same time  we sustain as fewer losses as possible  right so clearly from the ukrainian side  this ain't over yet yuri sack  advises to the ukrainian defense  ministry thank you so much for joining  us  thank you so much for inviting me  ukraine's president vladimir zelinski  says rebuilding the country will be a  colossal job so let's take a closer look  at the scale of the damage done so far  more than a hundred hospitals have been  destroyed damage to civilian  infrastructures running at more than an  estimated four and a half billion pounds  billion euros per week  thousands of kilometers of roads have  been wrecked and hundreds of bridges  blown up ukrainian officials put total  economic losses from this war at more  than 500 billion euros  ukrainian officials and international  leaders have begun a two-day conference  in the swiss city of lugano and to come  up with a plan to fund ukraine's  re